ial model and add  layers on top of it  the first layer will have is has 30  notes and has an activation function of  a rectified linear unit or raloo which  in the case of tensor flow that we used  before was the default activation  function then we'll have a nother fully  connected layer or dense layer with 20  new orleans this time also with a  rayleigh function and finally we'll do  our final mapping to the 10 output  values of 0 through 9 and have an  activation of the softmax which  basically just distributes our  probabilities across the 10 kind of  buckets and now we're ready to compile  our model caris uses this notation of  compiling a model as similar to when you  do something like a string builder or  something to just say I'm done put it  all together for me and we also apply a  loss optimizer and metrics for what kind  of values we want to get out of it for  what how to optimize for the best values  as well as how we want to measure loss  in this case we're using categorical  cross entropy because our outputs are  categorical and cross entropy in this  case happens to be a nice way to measure  our loss or error with our model created  we're ready to run training training  with Karis is as easy as calling dot fit  when we called that fit all we need to  supply are the training features and  training labels it's also a good idea to  supply epics and batch size so we can  control the training a little more in  this case we have supply that a pack of  two which means we'll go through the  entire data set twice over and we'll  supply a batch size of 128 this means  with that with each training step the  model will see 128 examples which  help guide it and to adjust its  parameters and so we can see here Karis  has some really useful outputs as the  training happens and it gives us a sense  of the progress it also then prints out  the bloss and accuracy at the end of  each epoch but seeing the accuracy at  the end loss at the end of training  isn't nearly as